{
  "workflowId": "300000331058565",
  "workflowCode": "ORA_GTM_RESTRICTED_PARTY_PREPROCESSING_ASSISTANT_TEMPLATE",
  "name": "GTM Restricted Party Preprocessing Assistant",
  "description": "Assists in improving Restricted Party Screening accuracy by preprocessing GTM Party (Contact and Location) data using AI-driven normalization (cleaning and restructuring data into a consistent format). This assistant standardizes names and addresses, removes noise (punctuation, abbreviations, diacritics), and persists normalized attributes so they align better with GTM restricted party screening matching logic, reducing false negatives and improving match quality.",
  "specification": {
    "jsonSchemaName": "Workflow.spec",
    "jsonSchemaVersion": "1",
    "inputs": [],
    "outputSpecification": " ",
    "agentsValueMappings": [],
    "dataPipeline": {
      "pipelineNodes": [
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Start of data pipeline",
            "name": "Start"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1775039188123"
          },
          "code": "START",
          "id": "start",
          "inputs": [],
          "type": "START"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Identify Contact XID"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1776282328797"
          },
          "code": "IDENTIFY_CONTACT_XID",
          "id": "1775039188123",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775039188125_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You extract the Contact/Party XID from the user’s message: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}.\n\nContext:\n- In this system, the DOMAIN is handled internally and must NOT be extracted.\n- The user will typically provide only the XID.\n- The XID uniquely identifies a contact within the user’s domain.\n\nWhat is an XID:\n- A string that identifies a contact or party.\n- It may contain letters, numbers, spaces, hyphens, or underscores.\n- Examples:\n  - CUSTOMER-ABC-123\n  - WQ_CONTACT_235\n  - JOHN SMITH\n\nRules:\n- Extract the single most likely Contact/Party XID from the message.\n- Prefer values that appear near words like “contact”, “party”, “gid”, \"xid\", “normalize”, or “use”.\n- If a value appears in DOMAIN.XID format:\n  - Extract ONLY the XID portion (ignore the domain).\n  - Example: MANUALSCREENER.CUSTOMER-ABC-123 → CUSTOMER-ABC-123\n- If multiple candidates exist, choose the one most clearly referenced as the contact/party identifier.\n- If no clear XID is present, return null.\n\nNormalization:\n- Convert the extracted XID to UPPERCASE.\n- Trim leading/trailing whitespace.\n- Preserve internal spaces, hyphens, and underscores.\n- Do NOT modify or infer missing parts.\n\nOutput:\n- Return ONLY a JSON object with exactly one key: contactXid\n- No additional text, no extra keys, no code fences.\n\nExamples:\n\nInput: “Please normalize contact MANUALSCREENER.customer-abc-123”\nOutput: {\"contactXid\":\"CUSTOMER-ABC-123\"}\n\nInput: “Normalize party gid: john smith”\nOutput: {\"contactXid\":\"JOHN SMITH\"}\n\nInput: “Use contact WQ_CONTACT_235 for screening”\nOutput: {\"contactXid\":\"WQ_CONTACT_235\"}\n\nInput: “Can you normalize the contact for me?”\nOutput: {\"contactXid\":null}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"contactXid\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Contact XID prompted assertion"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "true": "1774960168141",
            "false": "1776284888896"
          },
          "code": "CONTACT_XID_PROMPTED_ASSERTION",
